orted. The Company states it maintains an occupational health and safety management system covering all employees, workers and external parties who work at or visit its sites.","risk":"Workplace safety at manufacturing sites deteriorated versus the prior period"},{"note":"Management notes the FMCG sector is expected to enter a stabilization phase with growth projected to be volume-led rather than price-driven, with urban demand anchoring growth aided by premiumisation. Growth therefore depends on volume and mix rather than pricing, and management describes its outlook as only cautiously optimistic.","risk":"Consumer demand environment - shifting FMCG consumption and inflation-linked softness"},{"note":"The Company states it operates within the letter and spirit of all applicable laws, has set in place mechanisms for meeting compliance requirements with periodic monitoring to avoid deviations and regular updates to keep pace with regulatory changes, and runs recurring employee training on Global Anti-Corruption Standards, Prevention of Sexual Harassment, whistle-blower mechanism, conflict of interest, data privacy, data integrity and anti-trust compliance.","risk":"Regulatory and compliance exposure across a wide body of applicable laws"},{"note":"The Board's report states the Company has a very stringent system for assessment of distributors and vendors before selection, indicating that channel and supplier counterparties are a monitored exposure in the risk framework.","risk":"Dependence on third-party distributors and vendors"},{"note":"The internal controls section describes systems designed to protect the Company's assets and confidential information, including personally identifiable information, against financial losses and unauthorized use; the security section describes comprehensive security programmes at offices and plants with a regular security risk assessment, and reports no major security breaches or incidents at the plant during the Financial Year.","